Skills Hub Changelog

8/21/2025
- Updated logic used for dynamically loading grading results by implementing Flask Server Side Events (SSE).
    - Files affected: results.js, main.py
- Updated logic & functionality of logging to be controlled by `Flask` object and allow for storing of logs locally in rotating files located in new `logs` folder in `src` directory.
    - Files affected: All `.py` files, new `logs` directory, new files generated by logging: app.log, info.log, debug.log, warning.log, error.log

8/13/2025
- Fixed bug relating to the port service checker as it wasnt working as intended.
    - Files affected: globals.py

8/11/2025 -> 8/12/2025
- Added "Accessibility mode" to provide alternate method of viewing and reading content for those who might need it.
    - Files affected: globals.py, main.py, accessible.css, base.css, base.html, tasks.html, README.md, 

8/6/2025
- Made various updates to formatting.
    - Files affected: files.html, base.css, bookmarks.html

7/23/2025
- Fixed startup script bug that was preventing it from running correctly.
    - Files affected: globals.py, __init__.py, config.yml
- Fixed grading script execution permission check.
    - Files affected: globals.py

6/12/2025
- Added functionality to support the automation of hosting files relating to the "Mini Challenege" upon completing all the required phases.
    - Files affected: databaseHelpers.py, globals.py

6/5/2025
- Fixed bug relating to hosting files. 
    - Files affected: globals.py, files.html
- Edited default configuration of config.yml
    - Files affected: config.yml

5/5/2025
- Implemented additional functionality from CS update to edit logging functionality and adding an arguement parser.
    - Files affected: app.py
- Changed file name from config.py -> flaskConfig.py
    - Files affected: config.py
- Refactored functions.py by removing it and separating its code into multiple smaller files.
    - Files affected: functions.py, cron.py, databaseHelpers.py, grading.py
- Added typechecking where applicable
    - Files affected: __init__.py, cron.py, databaseHelpers.py, globals.py, grading.py

4/24/2025
- Added execute_in_docker function to manualGradingExample.py to provide functionality to execute scripts uploaded to server in isolated env.
    - Files affected: manualGradingScript.py, grading_README.md
- Edited runBeforeCommit.py script to clear logs as well to save space.
    - Files affected: runBeforeCommit.py

4/23/2025
- Added functionality to allow for user to upload file to the Skills Hub so that it can be used for grading purposes.
    - NOTE: This update did not test for creating in-game env. to execute scripts uploaded by user. That will likely require additional testing + updates.
    - Files affected: main.py, config.yml, config_README.md, upload.js, main.py, runBeforeCommit.py, functions.py, globals.py, tasks.html, base.css, manualGradingExample.py, 
    - Created directory: /home/user/skillsHub/uploaded_files/
- Fixed small bugs regarding how tasks are presented to user.
    - Files affected: main.py

4/21/25
- Edited logic behind recording solves in the backend Database so that it isnt creating as many needless entries, also implemented database lock mechanism to prevent possible race condition from writing to DB.(Thanks JB)
    - Files affected: functions.py, __init__.py, extensions.py

4/18/25
- Improved function logic and updated visuals.(Thanks JB)
    - Files affected: functions.py, base.html, home.html, base.css, files.html, services.html, __init__.py, globals.py, config.yml, services.html, results.html
- Implemented Bookmark QoL feature which allows for Devs to provide in-game resources/links to user.
    - Files affected: functions.py, base.html, home.html, base.html, base.css, info.py, bookmarks.html, config.yml, config_README.md, globals.py

4/16/25
- Added support for Multiple Choice question types
    - Files affected: config_README.md, config.yml, base.css, tasks.html, grading.py, functions.py
- Updated process of reading in tokens to replace file option with static so that tokens can be set in the config.yml file itself rather than a separate file.
    - Files affected: config_README.md, config.yml, functions.py, globals.py

4/11/25
- Implemented nginx redirect to have any requests to the URL skills without the domain .hub be redirected to the FQDN skills.hub to fix issue where results page wouldnt populate due to domain missing in URL.
	- Files affected: /etc/nginx/sites-available/proxy

3/28/25
- Improved method in which globals variable was passed to HTML pages. Previously it was passed in each return statement, now it is passed universally to all pages without needing to be called
    - Files affected: main.py, info.py
- Improved what pages were presented to user based on if the service was enabled or not in config. Additioanlly added different messages to pages depending if they had content to show.
    - Files affected: base.html, tasks.html, home.html, services.html, main.py
- Added two new settings to allow for enabling/disabling of presenting pages related to services and intro information.
    - Files affected: config.yml, base.html, info.py, config_README.md, functions.py, globals.py

3/21/25
- Added skillsHub.service config to repo and made small edit to require dnsmasq.service to ensure DNS is running prior to any startup scripts that may use FQDN for connections.

2/27/25
- Added runBeforeCommit.py script to handle cleaning up variouse files/configs on VM to ensure no corrupted files are committed.
    - Files affected: /home/user/runBeforeCommit.py
- Created function runSSHCommand to help w/ development of grading script.
    - Files affected: manualGradingExample.py, grading_README.md


2/18/25
- Added custom webpage to replace the 502 error page that can be presented if the user attempts to access the site prior to it being up and running.
    - Files affected: /usr/share/nginx/html/502.html, /etc/nginx/sites-available/proxy
- Updated and fixed bug related to functionality of how files are hosted. Before only files could be hosted, but now it supports folders being hosted and being able to access those folders recursively to download any files nested within.
    - Files affected: main.py, functions.py, files.html
- Fixed small bug that made it when there were 10 or more tasks, tasks would be presented out of order on results page.
    - Files affected: results.js
- Added steps on how the Skills Hub can assign static IP addresses through DNSMasq to remote hosts in skills-hub network without requiring the remote hosts to be unlinked.
    - Files affected: config_README.md, skills-hub.conf

12/6/24
- Fixed bug that would have mini_lab phase presented in the incorrect order.
    - Files affected: functions.py
- Added functionality to store data on all events (user interactions) that occur during the lab and store them in local DB.
    - Files affected: __init__.py, functions.py, models.py
    
    
Older:
- Added functionality to support grading of various question types rather than a singular one. Accepted grading types are 'button', 'text', and 'cron'.
- Added functionality to support two grading scripts. One to grade 'interactive' type questions that require some user input/data, the second to grade tasks that don't. This supports the change of allowing multiple question types. 
- Results page updates dynamically without refresh to pull most recent results.
- At first server boot, it initalizes a local backend SQLite3 DB and populates it with the questions for the lab configured in the 'config.yml' file. This allows for tracking of passed tasks and ensures if they are previously passed that they cannot be re-graded and failed.
